00:38:45,600 --> 00:38:48,760
Multiple granulomas
showing no central necrosis

725
00:38:48,760 --> 00:38:51,780
known as non-caseating
granulomas are visible here.

726
00:38:52,280 --> 00:38:54,960
And non-PCA and gynulomas
on lung biopsy are

727
00:38:54,960 --> 00:38:57,320
a typical finding in
pulmonary sarcoidosis.

728
00:38:57,960 --> 00:39:01,160
The last image on the
bottom shows asteroid bodies

729
00:39:01,160 --> 00:39:04,080
in pulmonary sarcoidosis,
and this is again a

730
00:39:05,110 --> 00:39:07,700
microphotograph of a lung
biopsy with an HNA stain,

731
00:39:07,700 --> 00:39:10,720
and you can see numerous
multi-nucleated giant cells

732
00:39:10,720 --> 00:39:12,980
are visible throughout
the microscopic fields.

733
00:39:13,140 --> 00:39:15,420
Two of the giant cells
contain star-shaped

734
00:39:15,420 --> 00:39:19,480
eosinophilic
intracytoplasmic inclusions,

735
00:39:19,480 --> 00:39:21,340
which are known as
the asteroid bodies.

736
00:39:22,280 --> 00:39:24,960
Multinucleated giant cells
with intracytoplasmic

737
00:39:25,260 --> 00:39:26,980
asteroid bodies
are typically seen

738
00:39:26,980 --> 00:39:29,920
in sarcoidosis, systemic
fungal infections,

739
00:39:29,920 --> 00:39:32,280
and foreign body
giant cell reactions.

740
00:39:33,960 --> 00:39:37,680
Most patients with
pulmonary sarcoidosis do not

741
00:39:37,680 --> 00:39:40,060
require immunosuppressive
therapy and can be treated

742
00:39:40,060 --> 00:39:42,660
with supportive care of
NSAIDs for pain relief,

743
00:39:42,660 --> 00:39:45,380
non-invasive ventilation,
and supplemental oxygen.

744
00:39:45,800 --> 00:39:48,460
Patients with symptomatic
progressive disease,

745
00:39:48,460 --> 00:39:51,240
persistent pulmonary
infiltration and progressive line

746
00:39:51,240 --> 00:39:54,140
of lung function can be
treated with immunosuppressive

747
00:39:54,140 --> 00:39:57,580
therapy first line
treatment is glucocorticoids

748
00:39:57,580 --> 00:40:00,440
dmars can be added if
patients are not responding

749
00:40:00,440 --> 00:40:03,520
to glucocorticoids alone
the immunosuppressive

750
00:40:03,520 --> 00:40:07,340
therapy of the dmars that can
be added include methotrexate

751
00:40:07,340 --> 00:40:11,720
hazothioprine chloroquine
hydroxychloroquine

752
00:40:11,720 --> 00:40:15,140
as well as biologics such
as tnf alpha inhibitors.

753
00:40:16,230 --> 00:40:18,380
Organ transplantation
of the lung,

754
00:40:18,380 --> 00:40:19,900
heart, and liver
may be indicated in

755
00:40:19,900 --> 00:40:22,140
patients with severe
refractory disease.

756
00:40:22,740 --> 00:40:26,720
In terms of complications
of sarcoidosis, individuals

757
00:40:26,720 --> 00:40:29,480
have an increased risk
of malignancy, especially

758
00:40:29,480 --> 00:40:32,820
lung cancer and malignant
lymphomas. They're also at

759
00:40:32,820 --> 00:40:35,780
risk for pulmonary
complications of bronchiectasis,

760
00:40:35,820 --> 00:40:38,760
pulmonary hypertension
due to pulmonary fibrosis,

761
00:40:39,100 --> 00:40:42,700
aspergilloma and chronic
renal failure. Chronic

762
00:40:42,700 --> 00:40:45,160
renal failure is
especially seen in

763
00:40:45,160 --> 00:40:47,620
individuals with increased
blood calcium levels.

764
00:40:48,620 --> 00:40:52,200
The image to the right
shows pulmonary aspergilloma

765
00:40:52,200 --> 00:40:54,460
and sarcoidosis and
this is a section of the

766
00:40:54,460 --> 00:40:57,080
lung that shows multiple
white lesions located

767
00:40:57,080 --> 00:40:59,840
along the bronchovascular
bundles and enlarged lymph

768
00:40:59,840 --> 00:41:04,040
nodes and this finding
indicates sarcoidosis.

769
00:41:08,360 --> 00:41:10,520
the overview of sarcoidosis can

770
00:41:10,520 --> 00:41:12,080
be seen in this schematic here

771
00:41:12,380 --> 00:41:14,000
sarcoidosis is a
very high yield

772
00:41:14,000 --> 00:41:15,880
topic when it comes
to board exams

773
00:41:16,180 --> 00:41:18,680
the etiology of
sarcoidosis is that it's a

774
00:41:18,680 --> 00:41:20,760
multi-system disorder
with t-cell dysfunction

775
00:41:20,760 --> 00:41:23,240
and non-caseating
granuloma formation

776
00:41:24,160 --> 00:41:27,380
non-caseating granulomas
can be seen on biopsy

777
00:41:27,380 --> 00:41:29,740
and that's the gold
standard you can also

778
00:41:29,740 --> 00:41:31,860
see bilateral hyalur
lymphadenopathy on

779
00:41:31,860 --> 00:41:35,440
chest x-ray and an
increased cd4 cd8 ratio on

780
00:41:35,720 --> 00:41:37,160
bronchoalveolar lavage.

781
00:41:37,300 --> 00:41:41,020
The systemic as well as
extra pulmonary and pulmonary

782
00:41:41,020 --> 00:41:43,260
symptoms can be seen in
the schematic as well

783
00:41:43,260 --> 00:41:45,560
and are important to know
and be familiar with.

784
00:41:56,130 --> 00:41:58,890
We'll now move into the
pneumoconiosis and we're

785
00:41:58,890 --> 00:42:00,930
going to start with
asbestos-related disease.

786
00:42:01,250 --> 00:42:04,430
The pathophysiology of
pneumoconiosis overall

787
00:42:04,430 --> 00:42:06,870
is that there's inhalation
of dust particles,

788
00:42:07,010 --> 00:42:10,050
phagocytosis by alveolar
macrophages, which

789
00:42:10,050 --> 00:42:12,130
leads to the destruction
of the alveolar

790
00:42:12,130 --> 00:42:15,190
macrophages, causing an
inflammatory reaction

791
00:42:15,190 --> 00:42:17,090
and leading to
scarring and granuloma

792
00:42:17,090 --> 00:42:20,950
formation. In terms of
asbestos-related disease,

793
00:42:21,130 --> 00:42:24,710
the etiology that
causes asbestos is the

794
00:42:24,710 --> 00:42:28,090
asbestos fibers in the
air. The population at

795
00:42:28,090 --> 00:42:30,830
risk for this is asbestos
miners and millers,

796
00:42:31,230 --> 00:42:34,010
brake linings and
insulation manufacturers,

797
00:42:34,590 --> 00:42:36,190
ship construction workers,

798
00:42:36,450 --> 00:42:37,590
demolishers,

799
00:42:37,710 --> 00:42:38,690
firefighters,

800
00:42:38,850 --> 00:42:42,310
plumbers, and roofers.
The typical clinical

801
00:42:42,310 --> 00:42:45,130
presentation is that symptoms
actually won't present until

802
00:42:45,130 --> 00:42:48,550
20 to 30 years after
initial exposure and when

803
00:42:48,550 --> 00:42:51,010
it does happen they'll
present with exertional

804
00:42:51,010 --> 00:42:56,430
dyspnea cough digital and
digital clubbing in terms of

805
00:42:56,430 --> 00:43:00,330
my microscopic findings
you can see asbestos bodies

806
00:43:00,330 --> 00:43:03,390
or known as perubinous
bodies and these are golden

807
00:43:03,390 --> 00:43:07,330
brown fusiform rods
resembling dumbbells and

808
00:43:07,330 --> 00:43:09,790
this will be found in
alveolar septae on histology.

809
00:43:10,130 --> 00:43:11,990
In terms of complications

810
00:43:11,990 --> 00:43:13,870
of asbestos-related disease,

811
00:43:13,870 --> 00:43:16,690
it can result in lung
cancer, specifically

812
00:43:16,690 --> 00:43:19,510
bronchogenic carcinoma
and mesothelioma.

813
00:43:19,990 --> 00:43:21,770
Bronchogenic carcinoma is

814
00:43:21,770 --> 00:43:24,020
more common than mesothelioma.

815
00:43:25,450 --> 00:43:27,890
Additionally, Kaplan
syndrome can be another

816
00:43:27,890 --> 00:43:30,390
complication of asbestos
-related disorders.

817
00:43:31,540 --> 00:43:34,510
In terms of chest x-ray
findings, there will be

818
00:43:34,510 --> 00:43:37,770
diffused bilateral infiltrates,
and specifically for

819
00:43:37,770 --> 00:43:39,990
asbestos-related disease,
this will be in the

820
00:43:39,990 --> 00:43:43,970
lower lobes. You can also
see interstitial fibrosis.

821
00:43:44,350 --> 00:43:48,390
Ivory white calcified
subdiaphragmatic and pleural

822
00:43:48,390 --> 00:43:51,910
plaques is pathognomonic for
asbestos-related disease.

823
00:43:52,130 --> 00:43:55,730
You may also see pleural
effusions on chest x-ray

824
00:43:55,730 --> 00:43:58,590
findings, as patients
with asbestos-related

825
00:43:58,590 --> 00:44:01,330
disease are at increased
risk of pleural effusions.

826
00:44:04,050 --> 00:44:07,590
The next pneumoconiosis
we'll discuss is silicosis.

827
00:44:08,490 --> 00:44:11,950
Silicosis is a
result of exposure

828
00:44:11,950 --> 00:44:14,150
to crystalline silica dust.

829
00:44:14,890 --> 00:44:17,490
Macrophages respond to
the silica and release

830
00:44:17,490 --> 00:44:20,090
fibrogenic factors,
leading to fibrosis.

831
00:44:21,130 --> 00:44:24,370
In terms of the population
at risk, the populations

832
00:44:24,370 --> 00:44:26,990
at risk include miners,
workers of quarries,

833
00:44:26,990 --> 00:44:29,630
pottery production,
sandblasting, and glass

834
00:44:29,630 --> 00:44:32,430
manufacturing, as well
as construction workers.

835
00:44:32,710 --> 00:44:35,050
In terms of the
clinical presentation,

836
00:44:35,130 --> 00:44:37,550
there's an acute versus
chronic presentation.

837
00:44:37,550 --> 00:44:39,390
Acutely, patients
will present with

838
00:44:39,390 --> 00:44:41,530
dyspnea, cough,
and pleuritic pain.

839
00:44:41,950 --> 00:44:44,190
Chronically, patients will
present with a chronic

840
00:44:44,190 --> 00:44:47,510
cough, exertional dyspnea,
fatigue, and weight loss.

841
00:44:48,510 --> 00:44:51,870
Complications of silicosis
include tuberculosis.

842
00:44:51,910 --> 00:44:53,950
It is thought that
silica may disrupt

843
00:44:53,950 --> 00:44:56,630
phagolysosomes and
impair macrophages.

844
00:44:56,790 --> 00:44:59,610
increasing one's
susceptibility to tuberculosis.

845
00:45:00,870 --> 00:45:03,090
Additional
complications include

846
00:45:03,090 --> 00:45:05,330
progressive massive fibrosis,

847
00:45:05,490 --> 00:45:06,910
respiratory failure,

848
00:45:07,330 --> 00:45:09,830
corpominelle, as well
as Kaplan syndrome.

849
00:45:10,430 --> 00:45:13,770
Findings on the chest
x-ray will show egg

850
00:45:13,770 --> 00:45:16,510
shell calcifications
of hyalur lymph nodes,

851
00:45:17,010 --> 00:45:19,140
rounded solitary
small opacities,

852
00:45:19,310 --> 00:45:22,230
and this will be found
in the upper lobes, as

853
00:45:22,230 --> 00:45:25,190
well as bilateral diffuse
ground glass opacities.

854
00:45:27,190 --> 00:45:30,370
The next pneumoconiosis we'll
talk about is cold workers

855
00:45:30,370 --> 00:45:34,130
pneumoconiosis, and this
is exposure to coal dust.

856
00:45:34,550 --> 00:45:36,710
Prolonged coal dust
exposure results

857
00:45:36,710 --> 00:45:39,370
in macrophages laden
with carbon, which

858
00:45:39,370 --> 00:45:41,670
results in inflammation
and fibrosis.

859
00:45:41,670 --> 00:45:44,210
This is also called
black lung disease.

860
00:45:44,680 --> 00:45:47,470
In terms of the population
at risk, this includes

861
00:45:47,470 --> 00:45:49,850
urban populations as
well as coal miners.

862
00:45:50,070 --> 00:45:52,710
The clinical
presentation will be

863
00:45:52,710 --> 00:45:54,350
chronic bronchitis
that progresses to

864
00:45:54,350 --> 00:45:56,970
progressive massive
pulmonary fibrosis,

865
00:45:57,620 --> 00:45:59,770
Complications of co
-workers pneumoconiosis

866
00:45:59,770 --> 00:46:02,770
include Kaplan syndrome
as well as anthracosis.

867
00:46:03,350 --> 00:46:05,870
Anthracosis is asymptomatic
condition found

868
00:46:05,870 --> 00:46:08,490
in many urban dwellers
exposed to sooty air.

869
00:46:08,830 --> 00:46:11,530
In terms of chest
x-ray findings, you

870
00:46:11,530 --> 00:46:14,330
will see fine nodular
opacifications and

871
00:46:14,330 --> 00:46:16,690
this will be found
in the upper lobes.

872
00:46:19,630 --> 00:46:23,170
The last pneumoconiosis
we'll discuss is berylliosis.

873
00:46:23,170 --> 00:46:26,970
This is associated with
exposure to beryllium,

874
00:46:26,970 --> 00:46:30,190
specifically in the aerospace
and manufacturing industries.

875
00:46:30,190 --> 00:46:33,570
Thus, the population at risk
is aerospace engineering,

876
00:46:33,590 --> 00:46:36,670
ceramic industries, dental
material production,

877
00:46:36,930 --> 00:46:38,890
nuclear and electronic plants,

878
00:46:38,890 --> 00:46:41,070
dye manufacturing,
and foundries.

879
00:46:41,250 --> 00:46:44,030
In terms of the clinical
presentation, patients

880
00:46:44,030 --> 00:46:45,930
will present with
progressive dyspnea

881
00:46:45,930 --> 00:46:48,670
with a few days of
high-grade exposure. In

882
00:46:48,890 --> 00:46:51,690
terms of clinical
presentation, they will also

883
00:46:51,690 --> 00:46:54,250
have non-caseating
granulomatous disease,

884
00:46:54,630 --> 00:46:56,750
which therefore
occasionally will respond

885
00:46:56,750 --> 00:46:58,590
to treatment with
glucocorticoids.

886
00:46:59,730 --> 00:47:01,650
Complications of
Borreliosis include

887
00:47:01,650 --> 00:47:04,570
lung cancer as well
as corpulmonale.

888
00:47:04,930 --> 00:47:07,790
Chest x-ray findings,
you will see reticular

889
00:47:07,790 --> 00:47:10,710
interstitial pattern in
the upper lobes as well

890
00:47:10,710 --> 00:47:13,830
as hyalurolymphadenopathy
may also be present.

891
00:47:17,170 --> 00:47:19,250
Overall, today
we discussed both

892
00:47:19,250 --> 00:47:21,410
obstructive and
restrictive lung diseases.

893
00:47:21,580 --> 00:47:24,230
We discussed the different
findings on spirometry and

894
00:47:24,230 --> 00:47:26,680
flow volume loops and how
they can aid in diagnosis.

895
00:47:26,790 --> 00:47:29,610
We discussed symptomology
and clinical presentations

896
00:47:29,610 --> 00:47:32,690
and the diagnostic testing
as well as findings.

897
00:47:32,690 --> 00:47:35,650
We talked about the
etiology and pathophysiology

898
00:47:35,650 --> 00:47:37,550
of both obstructive
and restrictive lung

899
00:47:37,550 --> 00:47:39,990
diseases and how that may
relate to symptomology.

900
00:47:40,230 --> 00:47:43,070
We talked about treatment
modalities, both pharmacological

901
00:47:43,070 --> 00:47:45,530
and non-pharmacological,
and they're important

902
00:47:45,530 --> 00:47:47,810
to be aware of in order to
treat patients accurately,

903
00:47:47,990 --> 00:47:51,390
as well as various serious
complications that can arise

904
00:47:51,390 --> 00:47:53,430
from the obstructive and
restrictive lung diseases.

905
00:47:54,070 --> 00:47:56,310
And this schematic
on the side is just a

906
00:47:56,310 --> 00:47:57,970
nice diagram that I
put here because it

907
00:47:57,970 --> 00:47:59,730
shows the interpretations
of pulmonary

908
00:47:59,730 --> 00:48:01,930
function testing and
where it may lead you.

909
00:48:05,410 --> 00:48:08,510
We now have some several
practice questions, So

910
00:48:08,510 --> 00:48:10,090
the next couple of
